  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'Pointing to a man, Neha said, "He is the only son of my grandfather''s only son." How is the man related to Neha?', array['Father', 'Brother', 'Uncle', 'Cousin'], 1, 'Neha''s grandfather''s only son is Neha''s father, and her father''s only son is her brother.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'A is the brother of B. B is the sister of C. C is the father of D. How is A related to D?', array['Brother', 'Grandfather', 'Father', 'Uncle'], 3, 'A, B and C are siblings. C is D''s father, so A (male) is D''s uncle.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'Introducing a woman, Rohit said, "Her mother is the only daughter of my mother." How is the woman related to Rohit?', array['Cousin', 'Niece', 'Daughter', 'Sister'], 1, 'The only daughter of Rohit''s mother is Rohit''s sister. The woman is his sister''s daughter, so his niece.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 1, 'P is the father of Q. Q is the son of R. How is R related to P?', array['Daughter', 'Sister', 'Wife', 'Mother'], 2, 'P is the father and R is the other parent of Q, so R is the mother and P''s wife.', 30, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 1, 'X''s mother is the sister of Y''s father. How is X related to Y?', array['Cousin', 'Nephew', 'Uncle', 'Brother'], 0, 'X''s mother and Y''s father are siblings, so X and Y are cousins.', 30, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'Pointing to a photo, Arun said, "She is the daughter of my grandfather''s only son." How is the girl related to Arun?', array['Niece', 'Cousin', 'Sister', 'Aunt'], 2, 'Arun''s grandfather''s only son is Arun''s father, so the girl is his father''s daughter: his sister.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 3, 'M is the son of N. N is the daughter of O. O is the husband of P. How is P related to M?', array['Aunt', 'Mother', 'Grandmother', 'Grandfather'], 2, 'O and P are N''s parents, and M is N''s son, so P is M''s grandmother.', 55, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'A''s father is B''s son. C is B''s only daughter. How is C related to A?', array['Mother', 'Sister', 'Grandmother', 'Aunt'], 3, 'C is the sister of A''s father, so C is A''s aunt.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 2, 'Pointing to a man, Kavya said, "His wife is my mother''s only daughter." How is the man related to Kavya?', array['Father', 'Husband', 'Brother-in-law', 'Brother'], 1, 'Kavya''s mother''s only daughter is Kavya herself, so the man is Kavya''s husband.', 40, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Blood Relations', 3, 'J is the brother of K. L is the mother of J. M is the father of L. How is M related to K?', array['Brother', 'Grandfather', 'Uncle', 'Father'], 1, 'L is the mother of J and K, and M is L''s father, so M is K''s grandfather.', 55, 'curated_blood_relations', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 1, 'Statements: All pens are books. All books are bags. Which conclusion follows?', array['Some bags are not books', 'All pens are bags', 'All bags are pens', 'No pen is a bag'], 1, 'Pens sit inside books, and books sit inside bags, so every pen is a bag.', 30, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 2, 'Statements: Some cats are dogs. All dogs are birds. Which conclusion follows?', array['All cats are birds', 'All birds are cats', 'No cat is a bird', 'Some cats are birds'], 3, 'The cats that are dogs are also birds, so some cats are birds.', 40, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 2, 'Statements: No apple is a mango. All mangoes are fruits. Which conclusion follows?', array['Some apples are mangoes', 'No apple is a fruit', 'All fruits are mangoes', 'Some fruits are not apples'], 3, 'Mangoes are fruits and no mango is an apple, so at least those fruits are not apples.', 40, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 2, 'Statements: All roses are flowers. Some flowers are red. Which conclusion definitely follows?', array['All flowers are roses', 'Some roses are red', 'Some flowers are roses', 'No rose is red'], 2, 'Since every rose is a flower, some flowers are roses. Nothing links roses to the red flowers.', 40, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 1, 'Statements: All doctors are graduates. No graduate is unemployed. Which conclusion follows?', array['All graduates are doctors', 'No doctor is unemployed', 'Some unemployed people are graduates', 'Some doctors are unemployed'], 1, 'Every doctor is a graduate and no graduate is unemployed, so no doctor is unemployed.', 30, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Syllogisms', 2, 'Statements: Some laptops are phones. No phone is a tablet. Which conclusion follows?', array['All phones are laptops', 'Some laptops are not tablets', 'Some tablets are phones', 'No laptop is a tablet'], 1, 'The laptops that are phones cannot be tablets, so some laptops are not tablets.', 40, 'curated_syllogisms', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Analogies', 1, 'Book : Library :: Painting : ?', array['Canvas', 'Frame', 'Gallery', 'Artist'], 2, 'A library is where books are kept and shown; a gallery is where paintings are.', 30, 'curated_analogies', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Analogies', 1, 'Doctor : Hospital :: Teacher : ?', array['Book', 'School', 'Student', 'Lesson'], 1, 'A doctor works in a hospital; a teacher works in a school.', 30, 'curated_analogies', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Analogies', 1, 'Cow : Herd :: Wolf : ?', array['Pack', 'Swarm', 'Den', 'Flock'], 0, 'A group of cows is a herd; a group of wolves is a pack.', 30, 'curated_analogies', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Analogies', 1, 'Pen : Write :: Knife : ?', array['Cut', 'Kitchen', 'Sharp', 'Steel'], 0, 'A pen is used to write; a knife is used to cut.', 30, 'curated_analogies', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Analogies', 2, 'Thermometer : Temperature :: Barometer : ?', array['Humidity', 'Rainfall', 'Wind speed', 'Pressure'], 3, 'A thermometer measures temperature; a barometer measures air pressure.', 40, 'curated_analogies', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Analogies', 1, 'Eye : See :: Ear : ?', array['Noise', 'Speak', 'Hear', 'Sound'], 2, 'Eyes are used to see; ears are used to hear.', 30, 'curated_analogies', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Analogies', 1, 'Carpenter : Wood :: Tailor : ?', array['Shirt', 'Scissors', 'Cloth', 'Needle'], 2, 'A carpenter works with wood; a tailor works with cloth.', 30, 'curated_analogies', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Analogies', 1, 'Water : Thirst :: Food : ?', array['Kitchen', 'Cook', 'Taste', 'Hunger'], 3, 'Water ends thirst; food ends hunger.', 30, 'curated_analogies', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Analogies', 1, 'Seed : Tree :: Egg : ?', array['Shell', 'Bird', 'Yolk', 'Nest'], 1, 'A seed grows into a tree; an egg grows into a bird.', 30, 'curated_analogies', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Analogies', 2, 'Kilometre : Distance :: Kilogram : ?', array['Speed', 'Mass', 'Length', 'Volume'], 1, 'A kilometre is a unit of distance; a kilogram is a unit of mass.', 40, 'curated_analogies', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Seating Arrangement', 2, 'Five friends sit in a row facing north. C is at the extreme left and E at the extreme right. D sits between C and B, and A is to the immediate right of B. Who sits in the middle?', array['B', 'C', 'D', 'A'], 0, 'From the left: C, D, B, A, E. B is in the middle.', 40, 'curated_seating_arrangement', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Seating Arrangement', 3, 'Six people P, Q, R, S, T and U sit around a round table facing the centre. P is opposite S. Q is to the immediate left of P and T to the immediate right of P. R is opposite Q. Who is opposite T?', array['Q', 'U', 'S', 'R'], 1, 'Facing the centre, your left is the clockwise side. Going clockwise from P: P, Q, U, S, R, T. T is opposite U.', 55, 'curated_seating_arrangement', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Seating Arrangement', 2, 'Five houses stand in a row. The white house is at the far left and the yellow house at the far right. The red house is to the right of the green house but to the left of the blue house. Which house is in the middle?', array['Red', 'Blue', 'Green', 'White'], 0, 'From the left: white, green, red, blue, yellow. Red is in the middle.', 40, 'curated_seating_arrangement', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Seating Arrangement', 2, 'A, B, C, D and E stand in a queue. B is ahead of A but behind E. C is ahead of D but behind A. Who is third in the queue?', array['B', 'E', 'A', 'C'], 2, 'From the front: E, B, A, C, D. A is third.', 40, 'curated_seating_arrangement', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Ranking', 2, 'Among P, Q, R, S and T, Q is taller than only T. R is taller than Q but shorter than both P and S. P is not the tallest. Who is the tallest?', array['Q', 'R', 'P', 'S'], 3, 'T is shortest, then Q, then R. P and S are taller than R, and P is not the tallest, so S is.', 40, 'curated_ranking', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Ranking', 1, 'Seven books are stacked in a pile. The Maths book is 4th from the top, and the English book is just above it. How many books are below the English book?', array['2', '5', '3', '4'], 3, 'The English book is 3rd from the top, so 7 − 3 = 4 books are below it.', 30, 'curated_ranking', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Inequalities', 2, 'If P > Q, Q ≥ R and R > S, which of these is definitely true?', array['S > Q', 'Q < S', 'R ≥ P', 'P > S'], 3, 'P > Q ≥ R > S, so P is greater than S.', 40, 'curated_inequalities', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Inequalities', 2, 'If A ≥ B, B = C and C > D, which of these is definitely true?', array['A = D', 'D ≥ A', 'B < D', 'A > D'], 3, 'A ≥ B = C > D. Even if A equals B, it is still greater than D.', 40, 'curated_inequalities', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Inequalities', 2, 'If M < N, N ≤ O and O < P, which of these is definitely true?', array['M ≥ O', 'M < P', 'N > P', 'P ≤ N'], 1, 'M < N ≤ O < P, so M is less than P.', 40, 'curated_inequalities', null, null, null),
  ('reasoning', 'Inequalities', 3, 'If X ≥ Y and Y ≥ Z, which of these must be true?', array['X > Z', 'Z > X', 'Y > X', 'X ≥ Z'], 3, 'X ≥ Y ≥ Z gives X ≥ Z. "X > Z" is not certain, because all three could be equal.', 55, 'curated_inequalities', null, null, null),
